.nh
.TH "PB-API-TOKEN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-api-token - Create, list and revoke workspace API tokens


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb api-token [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
An API token lets a script or service call the Paperboat API as you, in one
workspace, until it expires or is revoked. A scope narrows what it may do using
the policy's names; a scope never gives more access than you have. The secret
is shown once, when the token is created.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for api-token


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-api-token-create(1)\fP, \fBpb-api-token-list(1)\fP, \fBpb-api-token-revoke(1)\fP
